    "result_text": "All tests green. Here's a summary of what I changed to satisfy the redesign.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `customerCode` now has the form **`<REGION>-<HASH8>`** and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (the producer) \u2014 rewritten:\n- REGION = canonical region derived from the owner's postcode (falling back to city), via `Locality.of(postcode, city)`.\n- HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex characters (4 bytes) of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n- Sequence numbers dropped entirely \u2014 the class no longer scans the repository, so it's now purely a function of the owner's own fields.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 exposed the E.164 telephone normalization as a public `normalizedTelephone(String)` so the customer-code hash normalizes the phone the exact same way the duplicate-detection identity key does (spec's \"normalizedTelephone\").\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 added `of(customerCode, postcode, city)`: it reads the REGION straight off the `customerCode` prefix when present, so **locality now moves to the region-and-hash identity**. Legacy owners with no customer code still fall back to the old postcode-then-city derivation (via a `KNOWN_REGIONS` guard so an unrecognized prefix doesn't hijack the value).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now passes `owner.getCustomerCode()` into that new overload.\n\nValues that already read from `customerCode` needed no logic change and now automatically reflect the new identity:\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and its **Luhn check digit** \u2014 javadoc example updated to `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`.\n- **Create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 logs `customerCode`, confirmed emitting e.g. `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes \u2014 `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` (observed `NSW-16E6609E` for a postcode-2000 owner).\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
